WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.600 --> 00:00:06.624
Hi! Today we travel by bus and train.

2
00:00:07.024 --> 00:00:09.912
How do you get to work?

3
00:00:11.600 --> 00:00:14.440
This is how you get from A to B:

4
00:00:14.840 --> 00:00:16.912
the bus

5
00:00:17.312 --> 00:00:19.480
the underground

6
00:00:19.880 --> 00:00:21.952
the train

7
00:00:22.352 --> 00:00:24.544
the car

8
00:00:24.944 --> 00:00:27.256
the bike

9
00:00:27.656 --> 00:00:30.088
to walk

10
00:00:31.800 --> 00:00:35.048
After mit always comes the dative:

11
00:00:35.448 --> 00:00:38.024
I go by bus.

12
00:00:38.424 --> 00:00:41.192
I go by underground.

13
00:00:41.592 --> 00:00:44.528
I go by bike.

14
00:00:46.233 --> 00:00:51.113
At the counter or the machine you buy a ticket:

15
00:00:51.513 --> 00:00:54.617
A ticket, please.

16
00:00:55.017 --> 00:00:59.657
Where to? Single or return?

17
00:01:00.057 --> 00:01:03.185
To Cologne, return.

18
00:01:04.900 --> 00:01:10.644
At the station you hear announcements. A very important word:

19
00:01:11.044 --> 00:01:14.940
The train is ten minutes late.

20
00:01:16.633 --> 00:01:22.353
Listen: Lena and Mateo talk about getting to work.

21
00:01:22.753 --> 00:01:25.641
How do you get to work?

22
00:01:26.041 --> 00:01:28.905
By bike.

23
00:01:29.305 --> 00:01:31.449
In winter too?

24
00:01:31.849 --> 00:01:35.625
No, then by underground.

25
00:01:36.025 --> 00:01:38.097
And you?

26
00:01:38.497 --> 00:01:40.929
I walk.

27
00:01:42.633 --> 00:01:49.313
Now you! How do you get to work, uni or class?

28
00:01:57.000 --> 00:02:01.136
Great! Now you can:

29
00:02:01.536 --> 00:02:07.592
You travel by bus and train, buy tickets and understand announcements.

30
00:02:07.992 --> 00:02:10.112
See you soon!
